{
  "info": {
    "name": "Lab 3: scaling up",
    "description": "Service Discovery, round-robin load balancing, the circuit breaker, health checks with alerts, and the expiry of dead instances. Run it against the stack built from source:\n\n    docker compose -f compose.yml -f compose.local.yml up -d --build\n\nor the published images once they are tag 3. Folders 4 and 5 need the Collection Runner (folder 4 repeats a request; folder 5 waits about a minute).\n\nNot covered here, because they need a container stopped or killed: see lab3-tests.ps1 (Test-GatewayBreaker, Test-GameBreaker, Test-Expiry, Test-HealthUnhealthy) and the cross-instance WebSocket events (Test-GameEvents).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Health and load of every component",
      "description": "Grade 3 and 8: every service answers /health, with its load (`in_flight`, `max_concurrent`, `refused`). The Player copies have no host port; their health is read from the Service Discovery.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Gateway health",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('it is the gateway', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().service).to.eql('gateway'));",
                  "pm.test('reports its load', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    ['in_flight', 'max_concurrent', 'refused'].forEach(k => pm.expect(body, k).to.have.property(k));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{gatewayUrl}}/health",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Service Discovery health",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('it is the discovery service', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().service).to.eql('discovery-service'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{discoveryUrl}}/health",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Game copy 1 health (:8082)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('database ok', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().database).to.eql('ok'));",
                  "pm.test('reports its load', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    ['in_flight', 'max_concurrent', 'refused'].forEach(k => pm.expect(body, k).to.have.property(k));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{gameUrl}}/health",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Game copy 2 health (:8083)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('database ok', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().database).to.eql('ok'));",
                  "pm.test('reports its load', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    ['in_flight', 'max_concurrent', 'refused'].forEach(k => pm.expect(body, k).to.have.property(k));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{game2Url}}/health",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Player copies' health, via the Service Discovery",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const players = pm.response.json().player || [];",
                  "pm.test('at least one Player copy is registered', () => pm.expect(players.length).to.be.above(0));",
                  "pm.test('every checked Player copy is ok', () => {",
                  "    players.filter(p => p.state !== 'not checked yet')",
                  "        .forEach(p => pm.expect(p.state, p.url + ': ' + p.detail).to.eql('ok'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Internal-Key",
                "value": "{{internalKey}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{discoveryUrl}}/services/health",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "The Player Service runs as several copies with no port on the host, so its /health cannot be called directly. The Service Discovery checks every copy every 10 seconds; this returns the latest result of each."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
