    {
      "name": "4. Circuit breaker removes a failing copy",
      "description": "Grade 7 and 10, without stopping any container. A fake Player copy is registered at an address nobody listens on. The gateway adds it to the rotation, forwards every n-th login to it, gets 503, and after 3 failures within TASK_TIMEOUT x 3.5 its breaker trips and removes the copy, from its rotation and from the Service Discovery.\n\nRun this folder with the Collection Runner: the login request repeats itself until the fake copy is gone.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register a fake Player copy that cannot answer",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('breakerTries', '0');"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Internal-Key",
                "value": "{{internalKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{discoveryUrl}}/register",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"player\",\n  \"url\": \"{{fakeUrl}}\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Log in until the breaker removes it",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// the first time, give the gateway one refresh (5 s) to pick up the fake copy",
                  "if (pm.collectionVariables.get('breakerTries') === '0') { setTimeout(() => {}, 6000); }"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const tries = Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('breakerTries')) + 1;",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('breakerTries', String(tries));",
                  "const upstream = pm.response.headers.get('X-Upstream-Instance');",
                  "console.log(`try ${tries}: ${pm.response.code} from ${upstream}`);",
                  "pm.test('a live copy answers 200, the fake one 503', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 503]));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 503) {",
                  "    pm.test('the 503 came from the fake copy', () => pm.expect(upstream).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('fakeUrl')));",
                  "}",
                  "// 3 failures are needed; with 3 copies in rotation that is about 9 logins",
                  "if (tries < 12) {",
                  "    pm.sendRequest({",
                  "        url: pm.collectionVariables.get('discoveryUrl') + '/services',",
                  "        header: { 'X-Internal-Key': pm.collectionVariables.get('internalKey') }",
                  "    }, (err, res) => {",
                  "        const players = (res && res.json().player) || [];",
                  "        if (players.includes(pm.collectionVariables.get('fakeUrl'))) {",
                  "            pm.execution.setNextRequest('Log in until the breaker removes it');",
                  "        }",
                  "    });",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{gatewayUrl}}/auth/login",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "The fake copy is gone from the registry",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const players = pm.response.json().player || [];",
                  "pm.test('the breaker removed the fake copy', () => pm.expect(players).to.not.include(pm.collectionVariables.get('fakeUrl')));",
                  "pm.test('the real Player copies are still there', () => pm.expect(players.length).to.be.at.least(2));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Internal-Key",
                "value": "{{internalKey}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{discoveryUrl}}/services",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "The gateway log shows `circuit breaker TRIPPED ... removing it`, and the discovery log `removed player at http://127.0.0.1:9 ...: circuit breaker tripped in the gateway`."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Health alerts and expiry (slow: about a minute)",
      "description": "Grade 8 and 9, plus the expiry of instances that stop renewing. An instance named `postman-unreachable` is registered at an address nobody listens on and never renewed. The next health round marks it `unhealthy` and raises an ALERT, in the log and on Telegram; 45 s without a renewal later it is dropped (REMOVED on Telegram).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register an instance that is down",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Internal-Key",
                "value": "{{internalKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{discoveryUrl}}/register",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"postman-unreachable\",\n  \"url\": \"{{fakeUrl}}\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "After one health round it is unhealthy",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// a health round runs every 10 s",
                  "setTimeout(() => {}, 12000);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const entry = (pm.response.json()['postman-unreachable'] || [])[0];",
                  "pm.test('it is listed', () => pm.expect(entry).to.be.an('object'));",
                  "pm.test('its state is unhealthy', () => pm.expect(entry.state).to.eql('unhealthy'));",
                  "console.log(entry && entry.detail);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Internal-Key",
                "value": "{{internalKey}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{discoveryUrl}}/services/health",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "An ALERT line appears in the discovery log, and the same message on Telegram."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Without renewals it is dropped",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// dropped 45 s after its registration, on the next 10 s round",
                  "setTimeout(() => {}, 50000);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('it is gone', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.not.have.property('postman-unreachable'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Internal-Key",
                "value": "{{internalKey}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{discoveryUrl}}/services",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "The discovery log shows `removed postman-unreachable at ...: no renewal for ...s`, and Telegram a REMOVED message."
          }
        }
      ]
